A||N||18||AusFiero||Pictures of my other car.||||1||
Z||000000||AusFiero||07-22-2001||03:49 AM||||Well someone asked me to see what my other car looked like. I think it was Monkeyman. I think it was in email too but what the hell. Here it is.<P>It is a late 1998 Commodore R91 Police Pack. Got it with 40,000KMs on the clock as that is when our Police Force sell them.<P>Mods over a standard Commodore include:<BR>Lowered FE2 suspension handling package<BR>Commodore SS Seats but with standard model upholstery<BR>ABS Brakes (now standard in 2001 models)<BR>Extra interior lighting and different positioning. Why they needed so many lights inside I cannot guess.<BR>Radically tricked up and beefed auto gearbox<BR>Fully balanced engine, V6 in this case as it was a detectives car not a chaser.<BR>Police spec performance chip<BR>Traction control<BR>Independant rear suspension (not standard in 98 is now)<BR>Dual air bags (now standard in 2001 model)<BR>2 hidden but accessible fire extinguishers (in case we find any 84 Fieros   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> )<P>All I have added to it since purchase is 16 X 7.5 Commodore Calais Alloys instead of the steel police rims and 50 series profile tyres and tinted the windows.<P>Basically I hardly ever drive it. The wifes car mostly.<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/commodore1.jpg">  <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/commodore2.jpg">  <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/commodore3.jpg">  <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/commodore4.jpg">  <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/commodore5.jpg">  <BR>A guy in Australia fits the above 3.8 ltr engines to Fieros. He is too expensive though.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif">  <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.auto-alley.com" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A><p>[This message has been edited by AusFiero (edited 07-22-2001).]||202.139.20.3||reg||1
Z||000001||maryjane||07-22-2001||04:16 AM||||Nice car AusFiero,but SHHH,quiet, we don't use the F word and 84's in the same sentence.||||reg||1
Z||000002||AusFiero||07-22-2001||04:39 AM||||LOL Maryjane. yeah I know. But if us lot can't be light hearted about it who can. I know lots of makes of cars that had electrical problems that started fires. Happened to a friend here once with a particular local Ford model that used to prefer death by fire before 50,000 KMs.||||reg||1
Z||000003||mrgone||07-22-2001||09:44 AM||||cool aus. have you always lived in australia? you originally from there?<BR>what got you into fieros?<BR>show us more australian cars. they are cool<BR>any muscle cars?<BR>ive seen they still make last gen ford escorts down there||||reg||1
Z||000004||AusFiero||07-22-2001||10:07 AM||||Yep MrGone born and bred Aussie, lived here all my life. Kinda hard to leave a place that has 17 beaches within 10 to 40 minutes away (depends which one I chose) , windy coastal roads , A nice lake 3 minutes away , Mountains 5 minutes away (great Fiero roads) and not a lot of crime.<P>Wollongong where i live is actually an Aboriginal word for between the mountains and the sea. Widest stretch of land between them is 16kms narrowing down to mountains meeting the ocean. <P>What got me into Fieros, well I worked briefly at Ponti-World Australia and wasn't even real aware of them then. I was looking for a 65 Mustang Convertible and drove a Fiero when I was looking around for the Mustang. Mustang got shelved and I looked for a while until I found a t-topped Fiero for sale. Is only 3 t-topped cars in the country so I was lucky to get it.<P>I have another t-topped car on hold for me too at the moment, an 88 Formula. He is in no hurry and has kept it for me. Is real cheap too. The 3rd one is also now for sale, another 86 GT. Now if only I had the money I could own every t-topped Fiero in Australia.<P>I will scrape up some pictures of our muscle cars. Modern and old. Old favourites of the late 60s and early 70s was the Falcon GT, the Holden Monaro and the Valiant Chargers. Modern times is ruled by HSV Commodores and GT Falcons.<P>A HSV version of my above car can come equipped with a 300KW (402 HP) 5ltr LS1 engine and 6 speed maual transmission or a 5 speed automatic<P>Next year the Commodore goes coupe and is highly rumoured in the industry to be the new replacement for your soon to die F-Bodies. The new coupe has a different roofline and slightly different lines and by public demand is again to be called the Monaro.<P><p>[This message has been edited by AusFiero (edited 07-22-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Songman||07-22-2001||03:02 PM||||Looks a lot like a Saturn, Aus.. What exactly is it?<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Monkeyman||07-22-2001||06:41 PM||||Dale--It's a Holden Commodore.  Nice car.  Wish I had one.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Songman||07-22-2001||07:27 PM||||Is Holden another company or a product of GM or one of the others?<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000008||mrgone||07-22-2001||07:35 PM||||i think it looks like a mazda meliennia||||reg||1
Z||000009||AusFiero||07-22-2001||08:28 PM||||Songman. General Motors Holden. Or originally Holden Body Works in the 30's was bought by USA GM and virtually run into the ground when they moved USA executives here to try make cars for Australia. <P>The cars they bought out was inferior and not suited to Australian roads, mostly dirt tracks then. Inferior because of lack of research on local conditions and also bad marketting that did not appeal to the populous at the time.<P>In 1948 USA GM handed the reigns back to full Australian management and Holden has not looked back since. <P>The Commodore 3.8 ltr V6 for instance is almost an exact copy of the Buick 3.8 ltr but is different also in many ways internally and externally.<P>Our current batch of Supercars the HSVs are all fitted with Chev 5.7ltr (not 5 as I mispelt in  an above reply) LS1 engines. <P>We still also have our own local 5ltr Holden V8 but to compete with Ford and win the Bathurst 1000 GM decided to use Chev engines in all the top of the line performance models.<P>To show the potential of a Commodore I will quote this months Australian wheels magazine title after they pitched it against Audi, BMW and Jjapanese performance models in extensive track testing.<P>Bloody Noses, Broken Bones. HSV sticks it up Germany and Japan. <BR>Kinda says it real well   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Actually Jim Wangers (nice bloke Jim) of the GTO and The Judge days was over here for our nats the year before Jim Mattison came over. Wangers was so impressed with the HSV Commodore GTS he bought one and took it back with him. So if ever in San Diego keep an eye out. You may be suprised.<p>[This message has been edited by AusFiero (edited 07-22-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||kslish||07-22-2001||10:47 PM||||Doesn't that car come from the same platform that we in the States call a Cadillac Catera??<P>Ken S.||||reg||1
Z||000011||My7Fieros||07-23-2001||12:34 AM||||You're police dept sells their cars when they hit 40,000Kms? (Whatever that is in miles..not much though).<BR>My patrol car is a 99 Crown Vic and it has over 146,000 miles on it! (yes they get driven constantly)...and thats about the average!<BR>Interesting car, kinda looks like a Corsica.<P>------------------<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><FONT COLOR="red"><B><I>My 7 Fieros</FONT></FONT></B></I>||||reg||1
Z||000012||AusFiero||07-23-2001||12:38 AM||||Nope. Definately not. The Commodore is an Australian developed car only. The only country it is exported to mass is Saudi Arabia and that is only the luxury model Statesmans and Police cars.<P>Could possibly be a similar size but as for the platform, running gear, suspension etc etc etc it is truly Australian only.<BR> <BR>The only reason we are getting our Monaro back is because GM seen the 2 door Commodore as a great replacement for the F-Body, otherwise the numbers would be to low to justify the retooling in this country as we only have a population of 19,000,000.<P>GM US will deny all knowledge of that but it is getting to be a pretty commonly known fact on this side of the world. AUS GM won't confirm it either but just hint at it lots in motoring magazines.<BR> ||||reg||1
Z||000013||Pontiaddict||07-23-2001||01:05 AM||||The Commodore is based on the Opel Omega. (that would be a Catera here) But they are longer and wider and can't really be referred to as the same car no matter how much I do that.<P>Any pictures of the 2 door coupe Aus?<BR>I want to see what this thing's gonna look like before it hits the states. Although, I'm guessing that it will look different when it gets here.||||reg||1
Z||000014||AusFiero||07-23-2001||01:10 AM||||Yeah I have some pics somewhere of the coupe. Yes it iwll change radically for the states. Actually the Opel Omega is different as the VT model onwards Commodore was entirely re-engineered locally as the original opel platform of earlier Commodores was not up to scratch with our crappy roads.<BR>The original Commodore introduced  in 1979 was just an Opel. Things have changed radically over the years till it evolved as an individual model that GM is now looking at using elsewhere.<P>We have lots of rough roads and much of Australia is still dirt roads once you get outside the city limits so cars need to be built tough or they just fall apart. Many jap models are also re-engineered for Australian use only as the need lots of beefing up.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.auto-alley.com" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
Z||000015||Raydar||07-23-2001||10:08 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by AusFiero:<BR><B>...Things have changed radically over the years till it evolved as an individual model that GM is now looking at using elsewhere.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>One can only hope!<BR>If the Commodore SS was available in the states, I'd be all over it. I suspect that people would be lining up at the docks for them.<P>Can't wait to see the F-body replacement.<BR>Saw your other post. It looks a bit like a Cavalier to me, only larger. <P>If it has the LS-1, and GM calls it a Chevelle, they'll sell all they can build. <BR>  <BR><P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000016||lowfierogt||07-23-2001||11:15 PM||||AUS,<P>You know alot about cars.  I would like to see more pictures of cars from there.<P>Thanks..||||reg||6
Z||000017||AusFiero||07-23-2001||11:25 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by My7Fieros:<BR><B>You're police dept sells their cars when they hit 40,000Kms? (Whatever that is in miles..not much though).<BR>My patrol car is a 99 Crown Vic and it has over 146,000 miles on it! (yes they get driven constantly)...and thats about the average!<BR>Interesting car, kinda looks like a Corsica.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>40,000 KMS is about 26,000 miles and that is when the police sell every car in NSW Australia. <P><p>[This message has been edited by AusFiero (edited 07-24-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000018||AusFiero||07-23-2001||11:58 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by lowfierogt:<BR><B>AUS,<P>You know alot about cars.  I would like to see more pictures of cars from there.<P>Thanks..</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Lets just say I live and breath cars Low. I have been a car nut since I was 8 years old and never seem to have my head out of car magazines when I have some spare time. <BR>  Also I have worked in the industry in a vast variety of fields from custom cars, to racing cars to design of graphics for the countries major car manufacturers. <BR>Yep I LOVE CARS<P>I will definately post some more pictures of cars. Particularly our Japanese models. We have many cars from Japan that was actually developed here and are sold in Australia only. Japan can't even buy them.<P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.auto-alley.com" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
